 Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9ca7cd581a561a5d21c9d5aa6942a951a3fe5785f2914f2beb643758725b2533","compact":"667c69a9d5cc712d253a41c50bab06409e5805dc6413ce072335ff67fb59b268","nasal":"da9d37818de7d17fdb2acae90bc59484a3d2b9bda7b7985d054d9f7e72bad99d"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-88-16","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":88,"verse":16,"english":"O damsel, I take delight in this picturesque peak abounding in flowers and fruits, and frequented by various birds.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-94-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2088016","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"681d2f07d8e2882e1989b45e0a03a849abd7cfe93a7edb80ee0516ee52264c6a","compact":"89dd49a8a5d99035d96109c14632c212fc6821f0f799b2aa14cb1ca7f50c7ef4","nasal":"89dd49a8a5d99035d96109c14632c212fc6821f0f799b2aa14cb1ca7f50c7ef4"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-88-17","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":88,"verse":17,"english":"By this banishment of mine, I have gained two things, my father has maintained his truth in religion, and Bharata has obtained his dear interest.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-94-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2088017","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"033d2a40d81b57da992aa045c7926ab97f4270a82df3d81a04fe3f029ee8ada2","compact":"92ae459cbd1a6bd41eaf31941866a416229e069eb04f601fc3121526af2167f2","nasal":"ead502f2d8dd9d430425aec9b7b9cf23aa7072b46d41ab1d7f7916d05345eb5f"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-88-18","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":88,"verse":18,"english":"O daughter of Videha, are you being pleased on viewing along with me on Citrakuța, various objects grateful to mind, speech and body?","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.841,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-94-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2088018","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd61b5545adf18d854a70a3b96adde4fc82ac78d16e6977b076447ab6d8ee9d9","compact":"204d26d23414c4eb76537b5a378f085e70fe49b0993631869b8d54fd4b5a2533","nasal":"4ae1edb4aada9c53833a670e43a5cdc80b08a7f7e202fad9b81246374dd5d102"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-88-19","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":88,"verse":19,"english":"O queen, this abode in the forest like to ambrosia has been declared by those royal saints, my ancestors, as working out one's emancipation after death.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.852,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-94-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2088019","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3ae22627db37194f7f6702337b9bba8a291ea3b01fa9a334d70ad3701d2c12b9","compact":"cd9ffca96a12a9dfe04eb2a40edb0da5c174a9f3fdf5970164ab2987e246558c","nasal":"cd9ffca96a12a9dfe04eb2a40edb0da5c174a9f3fdf5970164ab2987e246558c"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-88-20","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":88,"verse":20,"english":"The giant crags of the mountain grace the place all round by hundreds; many and varioushued, blue and yellow and pale and red.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.85,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-2-94-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"2088020","sanskritFile":"Ram02.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"f001506b358d88c16d6a30d02e368056c7ccdc3de34b7afe3b92a0c1c4ed2983","compact":"c4093c5a08b4458470ff8d150acccea761e6a62724c68bee09c5da5ce3b55aa2","nasal":"fd9243ff8b704acbfa3efca329b15e031bf0d5697adc40dda50d6f42e60b3792"}},{"id":"VRCE-2-88-21","kanda":2,"kandaId":"ayodhya","sarga":88,"verse":21,"english":"In the night, the annual herbs by thousands growing on this foremost of hills, shine and become visible by their 